 ### Veterinarian directory
 
-<a id="req-vet-001"></a>
+<a id="req-vet-001"></a><a id="req-vet-003"></a>
 
 The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`.
 
+The directory is published twice: as the page staff read, and in a machine-readable form carrying the same veterinarians and specialties. Both are supported surfaces `[REQ-VET-003]`. Either can be narrowed to one specialty by naming that specialty in the request. The page then lists only the veterinarians holding it, still a page at a time, and the machine-readable form carries only those veterinarians `[REQ-VET-003]`. A specialty filter names the whole specialty, disregarding letter case; a partial name is not a match `[REQ-VET-003]`. Naming no specialty, or spaces alone, is the same as not narrowing at all `[REQ-VET-003]`. The specialty is named in the request itself, and neither surface offers a control for choosing one `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty named, when either surface is requested, then it publishes every veterinarian as it does today.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty veterinarians hold, when the page is requested for it, then only those veterinarians are listed, a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a narrowed page, when a later page of it is requested, then that page lists further veterinarians holding the same specialty.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty veterinarians hold, when the machine-readable form is requested for it, then it carries only those veterinarians.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty named in different letter case, when either surface is requested, then it matches the specialty as held.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty named as a prefix of a held specialty, when either surface is requested, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty no veterinarian holds, when either surface is requested, then the request succeeds and no veterinarian is listed.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty named as empty or as spaces alone, when either surface is requested, then every veterinarian is published.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
-2. **Known defect.** A second route returns the same list in a machine-readable form. Nothing consumes it, and it carries no requirement — see the Superseded list.
+2. A veterinarian holding several specialties is listed when any one of them is named.
+3. A specialty named with surrounding spaces matches nothing, because the whole name must match. See [Open Questions](#open-questions).
 
